# Electric hood roundover proposal — 2026-10-29

The owner rejected the angular hood and nose. A rounded front was built and checked, but concurrent work changed the same hood source and prepared-asset root while the final assets were being prepared. The current concurrent version retains the rounded front but reinstates a sharp hood-to-fender normal transition. To avoid replacing that concurrent work, the additional hood adjustment was tested in an isolated process and is **not applied to the current game source**.

The [isolated front-quarter preview](evidence/electric-roundover-proposal-2026-10-29/front-quarter-low-clean.png) and [side preview](evidence/electric-roundover-proposal-2026-10-29/side-clean.png) show the proposed combined shape. The [review patch](evidence/electric-roundover-proposal-2026-10-29/roundover.patch) applies to the concurrent source observed during this task; check it against the latest source before use. It changes the transverse hood section and its comment, leaving the concurrent longitudinal hood changes in place.

The isolated candidate passed 122/122 actual-mesh seam and winding checks and 64/64 existing nose and light checks at both detail levels. Hood-to-fender normals averaged about 9.8 degrees versus about 75 degrees on the current prepared model. The [test source](evidence/electric-roundover-proposal-2026-10-29/test_electric_smooth_seams.gd.txt) is retained here because it fails against the current concurrent model and is not installed in the normal test directory. Geometry checks do not establish a photographic match.

The experimental v3 mesh bake and earlier images remain as task artifacts, but the active source points to the concurrent `electric_reference_hood_v1` assets. Applying the proposal, regenerating prepared meshes, shadows, Garage assets and preview pictures, and rerunning the checks remain. No device test or deployment was performed.
